# Compile-time configuration for the MIDI firmware.
# Copy this file to `.config` and edit the values.
#
# Each KEY=VALUE line is passed to the compiler as -DKEY=VALUE.
# Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# MIDI_CHAN_START — the first (1-indexed) incoming MIDI channel the firmware
# responds to. The firmware always listens to an 8-channel window:
#   MIDI_CHAN_START=1  → channels 1-8  (default)
#   MIDI_CHAN_START=9  → channels 9-16
#
# Uncomment and set to change the default:
# MIDI_CHAN_START=9
